#26702
The Ash Plains~
   An expanse of grey-black ash stretches in every direction, broken only by
the skeletal silhouettes of structures long buried or destroyed.  The ground
crunches underfoot, and occasional jets of steam escape through cracks in
the earth.  Visibility is limited by the drifting grey clouds of volcanic
dust.
~
